{
 "_comment": "Provenance for the built-in food database in index.html. Each entry pins a food to its USDA Standard Reference 28 record (NDB number) and that record's exact protein value in g per 100 g. index.html rounds these to one decimal. test.mjs asserts the two still agree, so an accidental edit to a protein value fails the test suite.",
 "_source": "USDA National Nutrient Database for Standard Reference, Release 28 (2015, slightly revised May 2016) \u2014 served by FoodData Central as the 'SR Legacy' data type. Public domain. Nutrient 203 = protein.",
 "_note": "Foods absent from this file are marked est:1 in index.html: they have no USDA record and their values come from product labels.",
 "_crossCheck": "Every value here was checked against two files in the official SR28 release: the primary NUT_DATA.txt table (119/119 agree) and the derived flat file ABBREV.txt (118/119 agree). USDA's own two files disagree for 16 of 8,789 foods; NUT_DATA.txt is authoritative because it is the primary table and carries the sample count and standard error for each figure.",
 "_knownDiscrepancy": "Turkey breast, sliced, prepackaged (NDB 07081): NUT_DATA.txt says 16.33 g (n=7, SE 0.188, range 14.88-17.25), ABBREV.txt says 14.81 g. We use 16.33. Deli turkey varies a lot by brand anyway \u2014 check the packet if it matters.",
